---
/**
 * Preference — Economics-lens concept at Single scale.
 * Ranking under scarcity; economic face of the Vision Gradient.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Preference | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Economics lens · Single Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Preference
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					What the Identity values and is willing to allocate under scarcity.
					Expression of the Vision Gradient once Ownership has clarified whose scarcity is at stake.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Core concept under the Economics lens.
						Analogy, not isomorphism.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Value revealed under constraint.</h2>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/85">Preference</strong> is the ranking of ends that an Identity is willing to support with its scarce degrees of freedom.
					It is not abstract taste. It is the economic face of the Vision Gradient: what the Stem actually pulls toward when choice is forced by Scarcity and when Ownership has already fixed whose degrees of freedom are being spent.
				</p>
				<p>
					Under the Economics lens, Preference only becomes operative after Scarcity (relative finitude weighted by Mass) and Ownership (jurisdiction that attributes that finitude to a subject).
					Without scarcity, rankings lose force. Without ownership, there is no subject whose ranking counts.
				</p>
				<p>
					Preference is revealed in allocation, not in declaration.
					What an Identity says it values can diverge from what it actually commits under binding scarcity.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Preference is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Ranking under scarcity:</strong> ordered willingness to spend degrees of freedom on one path rather than another.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Expression of the Vision Gradient:</strong> the economic surface of what the Stem pulls toward.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Subject-relative:</strong> Preference belongs to an owning Identity; it is not a free-floating ranking of the world.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Revealed in allocation:</strong> the true preference structure appears where scarce high-Mass degrees of freedom are actually committed.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Preference is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not unbounded desire.</strong>
						Desire without scarcity is not economic Preference.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not self-declared Mass.</strong>
						Stating a preference does not create geometric weight.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not identical with the Vision Gradient.</strong>
						The Vision Gradient is the geometric pull; Preference is its ranking under constraint.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not fixed once and for all.</strong>
						Preference can shift as Mass, Metric Stem and scarcity profile change.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Surface the ranking</strong> actually revealed by allocation under binding scarcity.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Align declared ends</strong> with committed degrees of freedom.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Reduce dissipative rankings</strong> (high verbal preference, low owned stake).
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Keep Preference attributable</strong> to the owning Identity, not to foreign pressure or Account-level defaults.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/30 p-6">
					<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40 mb-3">Quick self-check</div>
					<ul class="space-y-3 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
						<li>Under the current binding scarcities, what does this Identity actually allocate to?</li>
						<li>Where do declared preferences diverge from committed degrees of freedom?</li>
						<li>Which ranking would change if the most binding scarce factor were relaxed?</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Related</div>
					<p>
						Prior: <a href="/framework/scarcity" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Scarcity</a> → <a href="/framework/ownership" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Ownership</a>.
						Next: <a href="/framework/opportunity" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Opportunity</a>.
						Physics parallel: Vision Gradient and coherent velocity along the Stem.
						Biology parallel: directed metabolism under finite energy.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/ownership" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Ownership</a>
					<a href="/framework/opportunity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Opportunity</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
